    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d461">

                <pb facs="0478" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg402"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 365.117/287</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Penfield to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 3, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1172. Department’s 1129, February 18. Information just received from central
                    information bureau of Red Cross states Frank Ghiloni wounded and taken prisoner
                    in October last, transferred to Mauthausen in November. He is now perfectly
                    well. Am awaiting reply competent authorities concerning his release.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Penfield</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
